{"name":"Old Yellow Bricks","hex":"#ece6d7","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"old","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-3 language code for Mochi."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of an object, concept, relationship, etc., having existed for a relatively long period of time.","Of a living being, having lived for most of the expected years."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/old"},{"term":"yellow","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The color of sunflower petals and lemons; the color obtained by mixing green and red light, or by subtracting blue from white light; the color evoked by light of wavelength around 580 nm; one of the three primary colors in subtractive color systems.","The middle light in a set of three traffic lights, the lighting of which indicates that drivers should stop short of the intersection if it is safe to do so."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a yellow hue.","Lacking courage."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/yellow"},{"term":"bricks","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["plural of brick"]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["third-person singular simple present indicative of brick"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bricks"}],"entries":[{"title":"Favourite Worst Nightmare","blocks":[{"text":"Favourite Worst Nightmare is the second studio album by the English rock band Arctic Monkeys, first released in Japan on 18 April 2007 and in the United Kingdom on 23 April 2007 by Domino Recording Company. Recorded in East London's Miloco Studios with producers James Ford and Mike Crossey, the album was preceded by the release of lead single \"Brianstorm\" on 2 April 2007. It was the band's first album with new bassist Nick O'Malley, replacing their previous bassist Andy Nicholson, who left the band shortly before the North American tour of the band's debut studio album, Whatever People Say I Am, That’s What I’m Not (2006)."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/a/ae/Favourite_Worst_Nightmare.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Favourite_Worst_Nightmare","wikidata":"Q955243"},{"title":"Old Yeller (film)","blocks":[{"text":"Old Yeller is a 1957 American Western drama film directed by Robert Stevenson and produced by Walt Disney. It stars Dorothy McGuire and Fess Parker, with Tommy Kirk, Kevin Corcoran and Chuck Connors. It is about a boy and a stray dog in post-Civil War Texas. The film is based upon the 1956 novel by Fred Gipson, who co-wrote the screenplay with William Tunberg."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9b/Old_Yeller_%281957_film_poster%29.jpg/330px-Old_Yeller_%281957_film_poster%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Old_Yeller_(film)","wikidata":"Q1851869"},{"title":"Brick","blocks":[{"text":"A brick is a type of building material used to build walls, pavements, and other elements in masonry construction. Properly, the term brick denotes a unit primarily composed of clay, but it is now also used informally to denote building units made of other materials or other chemically cured construction blocks."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/01/Brick.jpg/330px-Brick.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Brick","wikidata":"Q40089"},{"title":"Yellow","blocks":[{"text":"Yellow is a color between green and orange on the spectrum of light. It is evoked by light with a dominant wavelength of roughly 575–585 nm. It is a primary color in subtractive color systems, used in painting or color printing. In the RGB color model, used to create colors on television and computer screens, yellow is a secondary color made by combining red and green at equal intensity. Carotenoids give the characteristic yellow color to autumn leaves, corn, canaries, daffodils, and lemons, as well as egg yolks, buttercups, and bananas. They absorb light energy and protect plants from photo damage in some cases. Sunlight has a slight yellowish hue when the Sun is near the horizon, due to atmospheric scattering of shorter wavelengths."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d5/Cornwall_Daffodils.jpg/330px-Cornwall_Daffodils.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Yellow","wikidata":"Q943"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/a/ae/Favourite_Worst_Nightmare.jpg/250px-Favourite_Worst_Nightmare.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/a/ae/Favourite_Worst_Nightmare.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/a/ae/Favourite_Worst_Nightmare.jpg/250px-Favourite_Worst_Nightmare.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AFwn_large.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/56/TommyKirkFessParker.jpg/500px-TommyKirkFessParker.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/56/TommyKirkFessParker.jpg/1280px-TommyKirkFessParker.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/56/TommyKirkFessParker.jpg/500px-TommyKirkFessParker.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Promotional photo of Tommy Kirk and Fess Parker during filming.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ATommyKirkFessParker.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d1/Brick_wall_clo